<title>USA: Brent crude advances in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude advances in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude advanced in thin U.S. paper trading late on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>A full boat of August Brent changed hands at $18.61, up 13 cents from the IPE close in London.</p>
<p>A partial cargo traded at $18.59, up 11 cents.</p>
<p>Intermonth spreads were quiet, with July/August pegged at flat to five cents, August/September at minus 10/8 cents and September/October at minus 13/10 cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
